    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0b1f0b5c-aa89-5af6-bd8a-249514a1434e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -8 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $A?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_{1} &\\leftrightarrow R_{2} \\\\ R_{3} &:=R_{3}+(3)\\cdot R_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation $R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\n- The operation $R_{3}:=R_{3}+(3)\\cdot R_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -8 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -8 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{3}:=R_{3}+(3)\\cdot R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 4+(3)(0) & -8+(3)(-9) & -8+(3)(-5) & 8+(3)(-6)\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -35 & -23 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
