    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ab63c423-6158-580c-9e4d-c7814a848801",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 2 & -6 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $M?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_{3} &:=3R_{3} \\\\ R_{2} &:=R_{2}+(-3)\\cdot R_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation $R_{3}:=3R_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $3.$\n\n- The operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-3)\\cdot R_{3}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 2 & -6 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{3}:=3R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 2 & -6 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-3)\\cdot R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 2 & -6 & 5 \\\\ -5+(-3)(0) & 3+(-3)(0) & -5+(-3)(6) & -1+(-3)(3) \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 3\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 2 & -6 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -23 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
