      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 9 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 9 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_{3} &:=2R_{3} \\\\ R_{2} &:=R_{2}+(2)\\cdot R_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation $R_{3}:=2R_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $2.$\n\n- The operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(2)\\cdot R_{3}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 9 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 9 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{3}:=2R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 9 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 9 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=R_{2}+(2)\\cdot R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 9 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4+(2)(4) & 9+(2)(6) & -8+(2)(-2) & 2+(2)(2) \\\\ 4 & 6 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 9 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 21 & -12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
